  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_eeafb5e701844b1b8ff72ca6664503b1",
      "statement": "HueStream v2 wire format is pinned by HueStreamProtocol: 9-byte b\"HueStream\" magic, version 0x02 0x00, port 2100 (DTLS over UDP), colorspace byte 0x00 RGB / 0x01 XY, a 52-byte message header (9 magic + 2 version + 1 sequence + 2 reserved + 1 colorspace + 1 reserved + 36 ASCII config ID), and 7-byte channel records.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L22-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2648ee7bae843a06afd4a098c15805bbcf85d36bf3e9983e3ac74c5f0f86aad9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c309c1d85c146d69bc9de666ab09d7c",
      "statement": "The message buffer is pre-allocated once per connection at exactly MESSAGE_HEADER_SIZE + 7×N_channels bytes with the static header written once (magic, version, zeroed reserved bytes, 36-byte ASCII config UUID at offset 16); per-message updates rewrite only byte 11 (sequence), byte 14 (colorspace), and the channel payload, so no allocation happens per frame.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L205-L220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d45bd11970092d8cfdb93e5369a31489497b058690d5337fbd0e32c54e79986e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0c5ad54876b84893910fc0f1769c69c5",
      "statement": "connect(bridge) runs a strict sequence — fetch entertainment configuration (abort if missing), parse channels, initialize the message buffer, fetch the PSK identity, activate streaming via REST followed by a connection_timeout sleep, then open DTLS — and issues a REST deactivation if the DTLS handshake fails; any exception is caught and reported as connection failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L114-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb23ad3dcf946159d2e46b541629258dfa20083e1e3a4d0ff4ac2e130d5fccba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L177-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff1132617b827175eaad2056f82b603fdaae3d46f9c10b605b0968834f7ec9db:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e01acb5caad249948a87c24c8007befe",
      "statement": "The DTLS PSK identity is the hue-application-id returned in the response headers of the bridge's /auth/v1 endpoint (fetched with the app key as hue-application-key), falling back to the app key when unavailable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/bridge_client.py#L131-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c671e67f5d900d34215c8b48534b00f29fd5e62d95f4a25c358ac1986e3a4b3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L158-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c9f4edf97a364d02fbb3906a00e3e4ad4cad6892ae138aeebe16365bea675f29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4c3eed47ca384c678197d4da5e1d7141",
      "statement": "The DTLS connection is an openssl s_client child process, not a native socket: `openssl s_client -dtls1_2 -psk_identity <hue-application-id|app_key> -psk <client_key> -cipher PSK-AES128-GCM-SHA256:PSK-CHACHA20-POLY1305 -connect <bridge_ip>:2100 -quiet` with piped stdin/stdout/stderr, where client_key is the 32-char hex clientkey returned by the legacy /api user-creation call made with generateclientkey=true.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/bridge_client.py#L359-L378",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c899081cef6cf884139fe946f8dae9af7b50c6df364841fb60d417956052c3eb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L283-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2939f3c1a05222f00a5c5cd766c072f38615c8d1edd6249d33cfde23992973fc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f833e486e274ed7a5e7439ba11d62d1",
      "statement": "Because the openssl transport exposes no readable handshake callback, handshake success is verified by process polling: sleep connection_timeout (default 0.5 s) then poll(), sleep handshake_delay (default 0.3 s) then poll again; a dead process drains its stdout/stderr, prints the exit code, and is reported as failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L301-L324",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b912e5da8de0892fb6a61b11e4f404636f2d13c897d2950ce2f7f8f6c39da2f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_725f38f2abab4cfc96b490fca05457c2",
      "statement": "is_connected() returns true only when the _connected flag is set and the openssl process is still alive (poll() is None), so a silently-dead subprocess is treated as disconnected before the next send is attempted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L350-L354",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb88cea1858d04967d2c1d5313b8d595fe80c507ec067bb1f13b34223d5bb9a2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_29519e690ce34a71b117f56dd6f8cada",
      "statement": "The send path writes the message to the subprocess stdin with a flush under a lock; a BrokenPipeError/OSError marks _connected = False and re-raises, and the send_colors/send_colors_xy wrappers catch the exception and reset the flag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L356-L394",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3259e3af1cbc1013c012744e5dd1c1080675e9cdb823d1a3499c97a4f5ca9efc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L396-L413",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b31ab450165bfd1657dc8419a8f3dd0ae5aea62b4e5e3db993b1c1d471865e77:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1af3a4b016ca409783406644b96c93a8",
      "statement": "A native socket path exists as a placeholder: _dtls_socket is initialized to None with a \"Future: native DTLS implementation\" comment and _send_via_socket is implemented but unreachable because the socket is never assigned; _send_dtls_message raises ConnectionError when no transport is available.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L396-L422",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:129cc15ee0357fd4ef6e3da8dde3e153a45a56d4d607847d1c3527e49fe02a17:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L84-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7035412355ab74051b509eb5f6b6ac3080d4fe8e24bcd5983712995ee2322ce8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_658e9c5c86d84b2e80ce8757b188c48a",
      "statement": "send_colors_xy packs each channel record as >BHHH: channel ID, x×65535, y×65535 (clamped to 0–1), and brightness clamped to 0–254 then ×257 (≈65278, the protocol max); channels present in the configuration but absent from the input dict are zeroed (black), and the 8-bit sequence wraps at 256 after each send.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L446-L466",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31a26af02f0aade1a4ccaeb0fcf08679a177e0c30fdcf82fb18242253d91d4c5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L477-L483",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f252929ec3d2c8068a89077c10a99bd79059f47cdac2f1c43cda61ce72095685:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c5afb2761b94e7bb7e9844233c48b12",
      "statement": "send_colors (the RGB variant packing r,g,b (0–1) ×65535) is unused by the application — the sync engine's per-frame update path calls only send_colors_xy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/entertainment.py#L356-L373",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f66b9c3b40b7493b17fcc21f13a8cebfb612ae4d95682cbe8313e41a675a2dc6:"
        },
        {
